  "contract": [
    "A zero resource word returns null before reading the selector, even for an otherwise invalid selector. Nonzero resources require selector0/1/2/6; dispatch forwards resource and pointer to record word2 and propagates the full returned pointer. Native null slots3/4/5 are retained as null table entries, not invented replacements.",
    "Mode0 allocates732 bytes, returns null on allocation failure, clears the entire allocation, stores type0, calls graph initialization, copies word1e0 to238 and applies optional remapping from live parameters after callbacks.",
    "Remap stride is wrapping ((code>>2)-1)/groups. Zero groups execute no loop, matching native UDIV-zero/zero-iteration behavior without C division-by-zero. Each iteration reads its current target index and stores its payload pointer at context238+target*4. Remap aliasing and repeated targets preserve native order.",
    "Modes1/2 allocate568/572 bytes and store types1/2 before calling graph initialization. They do not clear allocations, consume parameter records, inspect initializer returns or invent failure cleanup.",
    "408 direct comparisons execute all216 native instruction bytes with independent allocation/type/zeroing/remap/return oracles, exact parameter-word read traces and provider snapshots. Cases include allocator/initializer mutation, remap aliases within allocated state, quotient boundaries, repeated targets, null resources and all allocation branches.",
    "128 complete HR constructor/allocator/teardown cases execute C dispatch, mode0/1 allocation wrappers, workspace, resource getters and queues. All primary/workspace/filter/graph/queue allocations release to the prior heap top."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The deeper graph initializer at340a0 and mode6 constructor5d01c remain unresolved. Their calling conventions are derived from observed providers; full graph construction, internal allocations and inference remain unproven.",
    "The mode6 record alone is preallocated through each real allocator and transferred through modeled mode6 returns. Modes0/1 allocate in C at native call points; the modeled deeper initializer leaves owned child allocations empty. Five external system/logging bindings remain in the fixture; ordinary successful lifecycles exercise graph ports only.",
    "Canonical resource pointers are normalized only in heap comparison and provider traces. Actual memory is not rewritten. Readonly resource spans remain unchanged.",
    "Selectors3/4/5/out-of-range with nonzero resources, invalid pointers, oversized/unmapped remap tables, physical faults, concurrency, cold floating-point activation, caller scratch and private frames remain outside proof. Zero-resource early returns are independently covered for those selector values.",
    "A subtraction defect initially escaped the first negative corpus because grouped division masked it. The final direct corpus adds18 exact quotient-boundary cases; all16 compiled defects are rejected by the strengthened final fixtures.",
    "The888-unit ld-r composition passes without failures or duplicate strong symbols.877 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged, tested object equals normal object, and no writable state added. One dispatch import replaced by two deeper imports, application73 to74; boot22.",
    "Source-plan/cache layout unchanged. Final executable linking/startup, complete graph dependencies, physical sensor delivery and boot remain open. Byte identity is waived; this build is relocatable composition rather than a bootable firmware image."
  ],
